| User model       | One person, one local profile                                      |
| Backend          | None                                                               |
| Database         | Local SQLite database                                              |
| Network          | Not required for core functionality                                |
| Currency         | BDT (৳) as the default; configurable later                         |
| Language         | English initially                                                  |
| Authentication   | None                                                               |
| Data portability | Encrypted or plain backup file, with user-controlled export/import |
| Design           | Minimalist, fast, accessible, low-clutter                          |

Important accounting rule: Wallet transfers are not income or expenses. A transfer moves money between accounts; only a transfer charge is an expense. Loan principal and repayments also need special treatment so that borrowed money is not mistaken for earned income and repaid principal is not double-counted as spending.

